\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Kirchhoff Current Law Validation at Metabolic Steady State (Theorem~3.3). (a)~Steady-state concentrations for the 10-node glycolytic circuit after numerical integration to convergence; glucose (GLC) dominates at ${\sim }1.0\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mathrm  {mM}$ while 1,3-BPG is the rarest species at ${\sim }1\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mu \mathrm  {M}$. (b)~Absolute net categorical flux $|J_{\mathrm  {net}}|$ at each node on a logarithmic scale; all residuals fall below $1.7 \times 10^{-6}\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mathrm  {mM\,s^{-1}}$, confirming that $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _j J_{ij} \approx 0$ at every node (Kirchhoff's current law in metabolic form). (c)~Three-dimensional visualisation of enzyme flux magnitude and steady-state concentration across the nine reaction steps, illustrating uniform flux (${\sim }0.100\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mathrm  {mM\,s^{-1}}$) through a heterogeneous concentration landscape. (d)~Enzyme-resolved flux profile showing all nine glycolytic enzymes (HK through PK) carry effectively identical categorical current at steady state, with deviations $< 0.002\%$.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:panel_exp2}{{2}{7}{Kirchhoff Current Law Validation at Metabolic Steady State (Theorem~3.3). (a)~Steady-state concentrations for the 10-node glycolytic circuit after numerical integration to convergence; glucose (GLC) dominates at ${\sim }1.0\;\mathrm {mM}$ while 1,3-BPG is the rarest species at ${\sim }1\;\mu \mathrm {M}$. (b)~Absolute net categorical flux $|J_{\mathrm {net}}|$ at each node on a logarithmic scale; all residuals fall below $1.7 \times 10^{-6}\;\mathrm {mM\,s^{-1}}$, confirming that $\sum _j J_{ij} \approx 0$ at every node (Kirchhoff's current law in metabolic form). (c)~Three-dimensional visualisation of enzyme flux magnitude and steady-state concentration across the nine reaction steps, illustrating uniform flux (${\sim }0.100\;\mathrm {mM\,s^{-1}}$) through a heterogeneous concentration landscape. (d)~Enzyme-resolved flux profile showing all nine glycolytic enzymes (HK through PK) carry effectively identical categorical current at steady state, with deviations $< 0.002\%$}{figure.2}{}}
